From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:41:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: Keep the picture we send upright as the phone turns

Teams carries no rotation with the video (its SDP has no
urn:3gpp:video-orientation), so the far side shows our picture as it
comes, and it was turned upright only for a phone held upright: with the
phone turned a quarter, Android showed us lying on our side.

The Phone app sends how the phone is held in changeMedia as
deviceOrientation (the shell's quarter turns, 0 top up, 1 left edge up,
2 upside down, 3 right edge up). teams_call_luna.c reads it
(teams_call_video_json_turns) and teams_calling_set_device_turns() hands
it to the media engine as "TURN <0..3>". teams_media (luneos-synergy-
connectors) turns what it sends by it; so does the PurpleMedia engine:
its camera head gets a videoflip of its own (pmdevflip) on the send
branch, turned the opposite way to the phone, as the front camera's
picture is not mirrored (teams_video_send_direction; checked on calls to
Android in all four positions with teams_media, which turns the same
way). The size we send stays, so a picture turned sideways goes out
upright with borders; the self-view is left as it is, for the Phone app
turns that one with the screen. A camera head made later starts turned
so.

Once droidvenc runs, its answers to caps queries keep anything in front
of it from being negotiated again, though what it takes never changes:
in teams_media on sargo the first turn stopped the camera with
not-negotiated. The size filter in front of the encoder (pmsendcaps) now
answers CAPS and ACCEPT_CAPS for it.

teams_video_send_direction() is tested in test_call_sdp,
teams_call_video_json_turns() in test_call_video.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
